      "id": "seg:paragraph:discussion:0008:0001",
      "blockId": "paragraph:discussion:0008",
      "type": "sentence",
      "source": "This method is similar to [`removeObject(at:)`](nsmutablearray/removeobject(at:).md), but allows you to efficiently remove multiple objects with a single operation. `indexes` specifies the locations of objects to be removed given the state of the array when the method is invoked, as illustrated in the following example:",
      "normalizedSource": "This method is similar to [`removeObject(at:)`](nsmutablearray/removeobject(at:).md), but allows you to efficiently remove multiple objects with a single operation. `indexes` specifies the locations of objects to be removed given the state of the array when the method is invoked, as illustrated in the following example:",
      "sourceHash": "754a7ae66846f6177b1dd86044c4affc42b3eced486a6e2d7f3a85e41e283a98",
      "translatable": true,
      "contextBefore": "Discussion",
      "contextAfter": "```objc\nNSMutableArray *array = [NSMutableArray arrayWithObjects: @\"one\", @\"a\", @\"two\", @\"b\", @\"three\", @\"four\", nil];\nNSMutableIndexSet *indexes = [NSMutableIndexSet indexSetWithIndex:1];\n[indexes addIndex:3];\n[array removeObjectsAtIndexes:indexes];\nNSLog(@\"array: %@\", array);\n \n// Output: array: (one, two, three, four)\n```",
      "documentTitle": "removeObjects(at:)",
      "framework": "Foundation",
      "ko": "",
